# Architecture

## Decision Tree Tool Loading

The core architectural innovation is a decision tree that dynamically loads tool definitions based on what the user is actually trying to do. This reduces initial token overhead from ~50,000+ tokens (all tools) to ~1,500 tokens (the navigator tool plus a few common utilities).

### How It Works

At startup, only a small set of "navigator" tools are registered:

1. **`tdx_navigate`** — The root decision tree tool. Accepts a `domain` parameter (`tickets`, `knowledge_base`, `assets`, `people`, `projects`, `reports`, `time`, `admin`) and dynamically loads the tool set for that domain. Returns a summary of newly available tools.

2. **`tdx_status`** — Reports current authentication state, loaded tool domains, rate limit headroom, and configured application IDs.

3. **`tdx_search_tickets`** — Pre-loaded because it is the single most common operation. Searches tickets with the full `TicketSearch` parameter set.

4. **`tdx_get_ticket`** — Pre-loaded for the same reason. Gets a single ticket by ID.

When Claude determines it needs KB tools (e.g., the user says "find a knowledge base article about VPN setup"), it calls `tdx_navigate` with `domain: "knowledge_base"`. The server then dynamically registers the KB tool set (`tdx_search_articles`, `tdx_get_article`, `tdx_create_article`, etc.) and sends a `notifications/tools/list_changed` notification to inform Claude that new tools are available.

### Tool Domain Hierarchy

```
tdx_navigate (root)
├── tickets (pre-loaded: search + get)
│   ├── tdx_search_tickets ★ (pre-loaded)
