# Tool Specifications (Phase 1)

## Navigator Tools (Always Loaded)

### tdx_navigate

Loads a domain's tool set into the active MCP session.

**Input Schema:**

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "domain": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": ["tickets", "knowledge_base", "people", "assets", "projects", "reports", "time", "admin"],
      "description": "The TeamDynamix domain to load tools for"
    }
  },
  "required": ["domain"]
}
```

**Returns:** A summary of tools that were loaded, including their names and brief descriptions. If the domain is already loaded, returns the current list without reloading.

### tdx_status

Reports the current state of the MCP server.

**Input Schema:**

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {}
}
```

**Returns:** JSON object with authentication state, loaded domains, configured app IDs, and per-endpoint rate limit headroom.

## Tickets Domain

### tdx_search_tickets (pre-loaded)

Searches for tickets matching the specified criteria. Returns summary data only — use `tdx_get_ticket` for full details.

**Input Schema:**

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "appId": {
      "type": "integer",
      "description": "Ticketing application ID. Uses default if omitted."
    },
    "searchText": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Free-text search across ticket fields"
    },
    "statusIds": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": { "type": "integer" },
      "description": "Filter by status IDs"
    },
    "priorityIds": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": { "type": "integer" },
      "description": "Filter by priority IDs"
    },
    "typeIds": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": { "type": "integer" },
      "description": "Filter by type IDs"
    },
    "responsibilityUids": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": { "type": "string" },
      "description": "Filter by responsible person UIDs"
    },
    "responsibilityGroupIds": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": { "type": "integer" },
      "description": "Filter by responsible group IDs"
    },
    "requestorUids": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": { "type": "string" },
      "description": "Filter by requestor UIDs"
    },
    "createdDateFrom": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "date-time",
      "description": "Filter tickets created on or after this date"
    },
    "createdDateTo": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "date-time",
      "description": "Filter tickets created on or before this date"
    },
    "maxResults": {
      "type": "integer",
      "description": "Maximum number of results to return"
    }
  }
}
```

### tdx_get_ticket (pre-loaded)

Gets full ticket details by ID including description, custom attributes, and attachments.

**Input Schema:**

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "appId": { "type": "integer" },
    "ticketId": { "type": "integer", "description": "The ticket ID" }
  },
  "required": ["ticketId"]
}
```

### tdx_create_ticket

Creates a new ticket. Requires at least one of: `requestorEmail`, `requestorUid`, or `accountId`.

### tdx_update_ticket

Performs a full update of an existing ticket. All writable fields must be provided.

### tdx_patch_ticket

Performs a partial update (PATCH) of an existing ticket. Only changed fields need to be provided. Uses the JSON Patch format expected by the TDX API.

### tdx_add_ticket_feed_entry

Adds a comment/update to a ticket's activity feed. This is the primary mechanism for ticket updates, status changes with comments, and reassignments with notes.

### tdx_get_ticket_feed

Gets the activity feed for a ticket. Supports limiting the number of entries returned.

### tdx_manage_ticket_contacts

Add or remove contacts from a ticket. Contacts are identified by their UID (Guid).

### tdx_manage_ticket_assets

Add or remove assets/CIs from a ticket. Requires TDAssets application access.

### tdx_manage_ticket_tags

Add or remove tags from a ticket.

### tdx_manage_ticket_workflow

View workflow status, approve/reject workflow steps, and reassign workflow steps.

### tdx_get_ticket_statuses / priorities / types / sources / forms / resources / response_templates

Reference data lookup tools for populating ticket fields.

## Knowledge Base Domain

### tdx_search_articles

Search KB articles. Returns summary data (no Attachments, Attributes, or Tags).

### tdx_get_article

Get full article details by ID.

### tdx_create_article / tdx_edit_article / tdx_delete_article

Full CRUD for KB articles.

### tdx_get_kb_categories / tdx_manage_kb_category

Category browsing and CRUD operations.

### tdx_manage_related_articles

Add or remove related article associations.

## People Domain

### tdx_search_people / tdx_lookup_people

Search and lookup people in the TDX people database.

### tdx_get_person

Get full person details by UID or username.

### tdx_create_person / tdx_update_person

Create and update person records.

### tdx_manage_person_groups / tdx_manage_person_roles

Manage group membership and functional role assignments.

## Assets Domain

### tdx_search_assets / tdx_get_asset

Search and retrieve asset records.

### tdx_create_asset / tdx_update_asset / tdx_delete_asset

Full CRUD for assets.

### tdx_manage_asset_resources / tdx_manage_asset_articles

Manage resource assignments and KB article associations on assets.

