# Claude Desktop / Cowork Configuration

### Claude Desktop (stdio)

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "teamdynamix": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["@chattstate/teamdynamix-mcp-server"],
      "env": {
        "TDX_BASE_URL": "https://yourschool.teamdynamix.com",
        "TDX_BEID": "your-beid-guid",
        "TDX_WEB_SERVICES_KEY": "your-key-guid",
        "TDX_TICKETING_APP_ID": "431"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### Claude Desktop (Docker stdio)

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "teamdynamix": {
      "command": "docker",
      "args": [
        "run", "--rm", "-i",
        "-e", "TDX_BASE_URL=https://yourschool.teamdynamix.com",
        "-e", "TDX_BEID=your-beid-guid",
        "-e", "TDX_WEB_SERVICES_KEY=your-key-guid",
        "-e", "TDX_TICKETING_APP_ID=431",
        "ghcr.io/chattstate/teamdynamix-mcp-server:latest"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

### Cowork (HTTP transport)

For Cowork deployments, the server runs in HTTP mode as a persistent service. The Cowork agent connects to the MCP server's HTTP endpoint.

```bash
docker run -d \
  --name tdx-mcp \
  -e TDX_BASE_URL=https://yourschool.teamdynamix.com \
  -e TDX_BEID=your-beid-guid \
  -e TDX_WEB_SERVICES_KEY=your-key-guid \
  -e TDX_TICKETING_APP_ID=431 \
  -e TDX_MCP_TRANSPORT=http \
  -e TDX_MCP_HTTP_PORT=3000 \
  -p 3000:3000 \
  ghcr.io/chattstate/teamdynamix-mcp-server:latest
```

